ounded by the agreement, referral, diagnosis and authorized scope."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0101","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 16.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 16.03-16.04","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-1600-collaborative-drug-therapy-management","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"B","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"The 24-hour notice rule does not expand underlying CDTM authority."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0102","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 16.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 16.03-16.04","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-1600-collaborative-drug-therapy-management","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"A","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"Gabapentin is Massachusetts Schedule VI while alprazolam is Schedule IV; retail CDTM bars II-V prescribing."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0103","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 8.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 8.05-8.06","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-800-pharmacy-interns-and-technicians","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"E","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"Clinical judgment about a significant interaction remains a pharmacist function."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0104","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 8.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 8.05-8.06","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-800-pharmacy-interns-and-technicians","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"D","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"A technician trainee may not perform final pharmacist verification."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0105","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 8.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 8.05-8.06","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-800-pharmacy-interns-and-technicians","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"B","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"Certified-technician Schedule II handling may occur within authorized scope, policies, pharmacist approval and supervision."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0106","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 8.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 8.04","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-800-pharmacy-interns-and-technicians","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"C","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"Intern practice requires the required registered-pharmacist-preceptor supervision relationship."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0107","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 8.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 8.04","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-800-pharmacy-interns-and-technicians","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"B","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"Internship credit is capped at 12 hours per day; the stated days yield 23 creditable hours."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0108","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 4.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 4.03","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-400-personal-registration-renewal-continuing-education-requirement","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"C","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"The pharmacy-law CE requirement is annual and cannot be cured by excess total hours in another year."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0109","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 4.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 4.03","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-400-personal-registration-renewal-continuing-education-requirement","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"D","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"Applicable compounding CE reaches pharmacists who oversee covered compounding."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0110","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 15.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 15.02","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-1500-continuous-quality-improvement-program","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"B","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"CQI requires assessment and prevention/system improvement, not incident logging alone."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0111","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 15.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 15.03","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-1500-continuous-quality-improvement-program","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"A","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"Initial QRE documentation is due within 24 hours of discovery/notification regardless of serious-event reporting status."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0112","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 15.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 15.03","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-1500-continuous-quality-improvement-program","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"C","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"The pharmacist must address the affected patient/representative promptly, minimize harm and involve the prescriber when judgment warrants."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0113","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 15.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 15.02-15.03","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-1500-continuous-quality-improvement-program","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"B","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"CQI requires systems-oriented assessment of causes and prevention."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0114","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 15.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 15.02","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-1500-continuous-quality-improvement-program","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"}],"Problem":"None.","Proposed_Answer":"D","Proposed_Rewrite":"","Proposed_Explanation":"Annual CQI education applies to pharmacy personnel covered by the regulation, not pharmacists alone."},{"Question_ID":"MA-Q-0115","Verdict":"KEEP","Severity":"Low","Existing_Answer_Correct":"YES","authorities":[{"authority":"247 CMR 15.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 15.03","official_url":"https://www.mass.gov/regulations/247-CMR-1500-continuous-quality-improvement-program","law_checked_date":"2026-08-14"},{"authority":"247 CMR 20.00","source_type":"MA_PROMULGATED_REGULATION","exact_section":"247 CMR 20.02","official_url":"https://www.mass.